# ADR: benchmark follow-up scope

## Status
Accepted

## Context
The 2026-10-11 benchmark (same model through two harnesses) and
the live zcode verification produced five candidate improvements.
Four look like repairs; the temptation is to guard the failure
that produced the most dramatic numbers.

## Decision
Accept only changes that state an existing invariant (prompt
line), add a bound (evidence cap), or respect an OS limit while
preserving a documented property (TMPDIR). Reject the verify
lint (deny-list of observed patterns) and the verify re-plan
path (model judgment steering deterministic control flow, new
loop state). Defer zcode parity knobs until a user needs them.

## Alternatives Considered
- Plan-time lint for controller refs in verify — Rejected:
  partial coverage, permanent surface, grows forever.
- Diagnosis-triggered verify re-plan — Rejected: new state;
  clever, not deterministic.
- Accept the blocked-with-diagnosis outcome as designed —
  Accepted; the work is making it cheap, not escaping it.

## Consequences
The unsatisfiable-verify class stays possible; its cost is
bounded instead. Revisit with evidence if it recurs among real
users.

